1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,159
Most tools start with a signal and ask what followed.

2
00:00:03,209 --> 00:00:05,215
Soundings works backwards.

3
00:00:05,265 --> 00:00:07,067
It marks every past rise and fall,

4
00:00:07,087 --> 00:00:10,493
then looks at what the readings were just before each one.

5
00:00:10,937 --> 00:00:13,413
Open Soundings in Angstrom Lattice.

6
00:00:13,463 --> 00:00:17,539
It shows the last checked research run, for crypto or for equities.

7
00:00:18,938 --> 00:00:20,731
The chart comes first.

8
00:00:20,781 --> 00:00:24,495
Price on top, with a small arrow on each close a rise followed.

9
00:00:24,545 --> 00:00:25,943
Below, one row per result:

10
00:00:25,963 --> 00:00:29,599
a dot wherever its condition held, coloured when the move followed,

11
00:00:29,619 --> 00:00:31,010
grey when it didn't.

12
00:00:31,466 --> 00:00:34,544
Point at any day to see its price, whether the move followed,

13
00:00:34,564 --> 00:00:36,033
and which rows were on.

14
00:00:36,083 --> 00:00:37,727
Scroll to zoom in.

15
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:41,990
Before rises lists what came before rises more often than usual.

16
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,314
Each result was found in the search years,

17
00:00:44,334 --> 00:00:47,311
then checked on later years the search never saw.

18
00:00:47,753 --> 00:00:52,362
Each card shows how often a rise followed, against that coin's usual rate.

19
00:00:52,412 --> 00:00:55,422
First in the search years, then in the later years.

20
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:58,667
The verdict says what happened on the later years.

21
00:00:58,717 --> 00:01:02,580
Held up. A bigger move either way. Weaker later. Or faded.

22
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:05,746
The failures stay on the page: they're evidence too.

23
00:01:06,183 --> 00:01:06,697
Like one?

24
00:01:06,717 --> 00:01:10,491
Open it as a Signal Set, then scan your assets with it in Prism,

25
00:01:10,511 --> 00:01:12,115
or use it in a funnel.

26
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:14,988
And How this run was done lists the settings:

27
00:01:15,008 --> 00:01:19,677
what counts as a rise, the coins, the years, and the rules a result had to pass.
